1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,325
Fell asleep scrolling on your phone and woke up unable to turn your head?

2
00:00:03,645 --> 00:00:05,705
A few daily habits might be feeding that.

3
00:00:06,105 --> 00:00:11,341
Looking down at a phone or laptop for hours keeps neck and shoulder muscles tense and slows blood flow.

4
00:00:11,661 --> 00:00:18,811
Low magnesium makes it harder for those muscles to relax, and coffee, salty snacks, and alcohol can make it worse.

5
00:00:19,211 --> 00:00:27,414
Drinking more than two cups of coffee a day has been linked to more frequent neck and shoulder pain, possibly because caffeine keeps muscles braced and mildly dehydrated.

6
00:00:27,734 --> 00:00:30,862
Cutting back to one cup and drinking extra water may help ease that.

7
00:00:31,353 --> 00:00:38,565
Fast food and salty snacks can crowd out magnesium-rich whole foods, leaving you short on the mineral your muscles need to relax.

8
00:00:39,138 --> 00:00:43,008
Alcohol drains magnesium and disrupts the deep sleep your muscles need to recover overnight.

9
00:00:43,495 --> 00:00:50,322
Cut back on coffee, salty snacks, and alcohol, and add more whole foods like chickpeas and salmon to your meals for their magnesium and omega-3s.
